{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>For the house of Levi.</b> The staff of the prince himself, and after it, with it, the staff of Aaron, staff of the house of Levi." "<b>And yielded.</b> From the root of <i>and the child grew and was weaned</i>. And many said on account of almonds, for the staff was from the species of the almond tree, and it is no proof, and it is a midrashic approach, for <i>shkedim</i> [almonds] is as <i>for I am watchful</i> [shoked]."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:12.985850860Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}